FULLTEXT[7].pages.push(...[{"page": 16, "zh": "### Table 3. 不同 Bacterial Meningitis 族群的常見 Pathogens 與對應建議 Empiric Therapy\n|Patient group|常見 pathogens|建議 empiric therapy|\n|---|---|---|\n|Community-acquired：18–50 歲|N. meningitidis、S. pneumoniae|Vancomycin + third-generation cephalosporin（如 ceftriaxone）|\n|Community-acquired：>50 歲，或任何年齡有 predisposing condition a|N. meningitidis、S. pneumoniae、L. monocytogenes、H. influenzae、aerobic GNB（如 E. coli）|Vancomycin + third-generation cephalosporin（如 ceftriaxone）+ ampicillin|\n|Health care–associated／nosocomial：basilar skull fracture，與 sinuses 或 oropharynx 相通|S. pneumoniae、H. influenzae、group A β-hemolytic streptococci|Vancomycin + third-generation cephalosporin（如 ceftriaxone）|\n|Health care–associated／nosocomial：penetrating trauma|S. aureus、CoNS、aerobic enteric（如 E. coli）及 non-lactose-fermenting（如 P. aeruginosa）gram-negative bacilli|Vancomycin + cefepime 或 ceftazidime 或 meropenem|\n|Post-neurosurgery|Aerobic enteric（如 E. coli）與 non-lactose-fermenting（如 P. aeruginosa）gram-negative bacilli、S. aureus、CoNS|Vancomycin + cefepime 或 ceftazidime 或 meropenem|\n|CSF shunt|Aerobic enteric（如 E. coli）與 non-lactose-fermenting（如 P. aeruginosa）gram-negative bacilli、S. aureus、Propionibacterium acnes|Vancomycin + cefepime 或 ceftazidime 或 meropenem|\na. Altered immune status、alcoholism。\nCoNS = coagulase-negative staphylococci；GNB = gram-negative bacteria。\n### Table 4. 部分 Antibiotics 的 CSF Penetration 與 Meningitis Dosages\n|Agent|CSF penetration，占 serum concentration 的 %|Meningitis dosage|\n|---|---|---|\n|Amikacin|低|Conventional：10–15 mg/kg a IV q8–12hr；extended interval：20–25 mg/kg a IV 每日一次；intraventricular：30 mg 每日一次|\n|Ampicillin|13–14|2 g IV q4hr|\n|Cefazolin|8–15|2 g IV q8hr|\n|Cefepime|10–20|2 g IV q8hr|\n|Cefotaxime|10–12|2 g IV q4hr|\n|Ceftazidime|30–40|2 g IV q8hr|\n|Ceftriaxone|8–12|2 g IV q12hr|\n|Ciprofloxacin|20–25|400 mg IV q8hr|\n|Colistin|低|Intraventricular：10 mg 每日一次|\n|Meropenem|6–21|2 g IV q8hr，可考慮每次輸注 3 小時的 extended infusions|", "en": "Table 3. Common Pathogens Seen in Different Bacterial Meningitis Populations and the Corresponding Recommended Empiric Therapy Patient Group Common Pathogens Recommended Empiric Therapy Community-Acquired Pathogens 18–50 yr N. meningitidis, S. pneumoniae Vancomycin + third-generation cephalosporin (e.g., ceftriaxone) > 50 yr or any age with predisposing conditiona\n\nN. meningitidis, S. pneumoniae,\n\nL. monocytogenes, H. inÞuenzae, aerobic GNB (e.g., E. coli) Vancomycin + third-generation cephalosporin (e.g., ceftriaxone) + ampicillin Health care–associated or nosocomial Basilar skull fracture (communication with sinuses or oropharynx)\n\nS. pneumoniae; H. inÞuenzae; group A β-hemolytic streptococci Vancomycin + third-generation cephalosporin (e.g., ceftriaxone) Health care–associated or nosocomial Penetrating trauma\n\nS. aureus, CoNS, aerobic enteric (e.g., E. coli) and non–lactose-fermenting (e.g., P. aeruginosa) gram-negative bacilli Vancomycin + cefepime or ceftazidime or meropenem Post-neurosurgery Aerobic enteric (e.g., E. coli) and non–lactosefermenting (e.g., P. aeruginosa) gram-negative bacilli, S. aureus, CoNS Vancomycin + cefepime or ceftazidime or meropenem CSF shunt Aerobic enteric (e.g., E. coli) and non–lactosefermenting (e.g., P. aeruginosa) gram-negative bacilli, S. aureus, Propionibacterium acnes Vancomycin + cefepime or ceftazidime or meropenem aAltered immune status, alcoholism CoNS = coagulase-negative staphylococci; GNB = gram-negative bacteria.\n\nTable 4. Selected Antibiotic CSF Penetration and Dosages for Meningitis Agent CSF Penetration, % of Serum Concentration Dosage for Meningitis Amikacin Low Conventional: 10–15 mg/kga IV q8–12hr Extended interval: 20–25 mg/kga IV once daily Intraventricular: 30 mg once daily Ampicillin 13–14 2 g IV q4hr Cefazolin 8–15 2 g IV q8hr Cefepime 10–20 2 g IV q8hr Cefotaxime 10–12 2 g IV q4hr Ceftazidime 30–40 2 g IV q8hr Ceftriaxone 8–12 2 g IV q12hr Ciprofloxacin 20–25 400 mg IV q8hr Colistin Low Intraventricular: 10 mg once daily Meropenem 6–21 2 g IV q8hr (extended infusions over 3 hr may be considered)"}, {"page": 17, "zh": "### Table 4. 部分 Antibiotics 的 CSF Penetration 與 Meningitis Dosages（續）\n|Agent|CSF penetration，占 serum concentration 的 %|Meningitis dosage|\n|---|---|---|\n|Nafcillin|1–2.5|2 g IV q4hr|\n|Piperacillin/tazobactam|20–30|因 tazobactam penetration 低，不建議|\n|Tobramycin|10–20|Conventional：2–3 mg/kg IV q8–12hr；extended interval：5–7 mg/kg IV 每日一次；intraventricular：10–20 mg 每日一次|\n|Vancomycin|30|15–20 mg/kg IV q8–12hr；intraventricular：10–20 mg 每日一次|\na. 使用 IBW；若 actual body weight 超過 IBW 20%，則使用 adjusted body weight = IBW + 0.4 ×（actual weight − IBW）。\nIV = intravenous；q = 每隔。\n## Patient Case\n2. H.K. 為 42 歲女性，由丈夫陪同，從家中至 emergency department，出現 mental status changes、lethargy 與 temperature 102.9°F（39.4°C）。丈夫表示，24 小時前有 severe headache。沒有重要 medical history。Diagnostic workup results 高度懷疑 meningitis。進行 lumbar puncture 時，發現 initial pressure 高。H.K. 初始最適當處置為何？\n   A. 給予 dexamethasone 0.15 mg/kg IV。\n   B. 等待 laboratory 與 microbiologic analysis。\n   C. 開始 empiric ceftriaxone 與 vancomycin。\n   D. 開始 empiric ampicillin、cefepime 與 vancomycin。\n## III. ANTIMICROBIAL STEWARDSHIP\nA. 目標：使 clinical outcomes 最佳化，同時減少 antimicrobial use 的非預期後果，包括 antimicrobial resistance 出現與 adverse drug reactions。此外，以負責任的方式使用 antimicrobial agents，應降低 treatment 的 overall costs。\n   1. Antibiotics 是造成 adverse effects 的第二常見 drug class。\n   2. Antibiotics 是最常與 prescribing errors 相關的 medication class。\n   3. 藉最佳化 therapy 降低 antimicrobial resistance，應能帶來可量測的 patient-level benefits，因研究顯示 antimicrobial resistance 對數種 clinical outcomes 有負面影響。\n   4. 2018 年，CMS 完成規定，要求所有參與 Medicaid／Medicare services 的 acute care hospitals，實施 antimicrobial stewardship programs。", "en": "Table 4. Selected Antibiotic CSF Penetration and Dosages for Meningitis (continued) Agent CSF Penetration, % of Serum Concentration Dosage for Meningitis Nafcillin 1–2.5 2 g IV q4hr Piperacillin/tazobactam 20–30 Not recommended because of low penetration of tazobactam Tobramycin 10–20 Conventional 2–3 mg/kg IV q8–12hr Extended interval: 5–7 mg/kg IV once daily Intraventricular 10–20 mg once daily Vancomycin 30 15–20 mg/kg IV q8–12hr Intraventricular 10–20 mg once daily a Use IBW unless actual body weight is > 20% of IBW. If actual body weight is >20% IBW use adjusted body weight. Adjusted body weight = IBW + 0.4 (actual weight − IBW). IV = intravenous(ly); q = every\n\nPatient Case\n\n2. H.K. is a 42-year-old woman who presents with her husband to the emergency department from home with mental status changes, lethargy, and a temperature of 102.9°F (39.4°C). Her husband reports that she had a severe headache 24 hours earlier. She has no significant medical history. Diagnostic workup results are highly suggestive of meningitis. A lumbar puncture is performed, during which a high initial pressure is noted. Which intervention would be best initially for H.K.?\n\nA. Administer dexamethasone 0.15 mg/kg intravenously.\n\nB. Await laboratory and microbiologic analysis.\n\nC. Initiate empiric ceftriaxone and vancomycin.\n\nD. Initiate empiric ampicillin, cefepime, and vancomycin.\n\nIII. ANTIMICROBIAL STEWARDSHIP\n\nA. Goals: To optimize clinical outcomes while minimizing unintended consequences of antimicrobial use, which include the emergence of antimicrobial resistance and adverse drug reactions. In addition, a responsible approach to the use of antimicrobial agents should reduce the overall costs associated with treatment.\n\n1. Antibiotics are the second most common class of drugs that cause adverse effects.\n\n2. Antibiotics are the most common class of medication to be associated with prescribing errors.\n\n3. Minimizing antimicrobial resistance by optimizing therapy should lead to measurable benefits at the patient level because studies have shown the negative effect of antimicrobial resistance on several clinical outcomes.\n\n4. In 2018, CMS finalized a rule that requires all acute care hospitals participating in Medicaid/Medicare services to implement antimicrobial stewardship programs."}, {"page": 18, "zh": "5. 2019 年，CDC 更新 hospital core elements，以反映 antimicrobial stewardship 的新證據。主要更新包括 hospital leadership commitment、accountability、pharmacy expertise、tracking、reporting 與 education。\nB. Antimicrobial Stewardship 定義：透過 multidisciplinary、協調一致的 interventions，改善並量測 antimicrobial agents 的適當使用，促進選擇最佳 antimicrobial drug regimen，包括 dosing、duration 與 route of administration。\n   1. Multidisciplinary team 的 core members 應包括 infectious diseases physician、clinical pharmacist、clinical microbiologist、information systems specialist、infection control professional、nurse 與 hospital epidemiologist。\n   2. ICU 常需 broad-spectrum antimicrobials，提供早期有效 therapy；但持續使用可能選出 pathogenic organisms（如 C. difficile、Candida spp.），造成 nephrotoxicity，並使 resistance 出現。\nC. Critical Care Pharmacists：適合提供 antimicrobial therapy 指導，包括迅速選擇適當 initial agents、積極 dosing 以最佳化 PD、解讀 microbiological evidence、適當 de-escalation、監測 response 與可能 adverse effects，以及決定適當 treatment duration。\n   1. Critical care pharmacists 可作為 multidisciplinary antibiotic stewardship team 成員積極參與，或執行不同的 stewardship roles 與 activities。\n   2. 可透過正式 pathways 或 everyday clinical interventions 進行的 core activities：\n      a. 結合 active intervention 的 education：解讀 rapid identification tests 與 susceptibility testing。\n      b. Guidelines 與 clinical pathway development。近期 IDSA guidelines 建議，以 facility-specific clinical practice guidelines 或 algorithms，作為標準化 prescribing practices 的有效方式。\n      c. Streamlining 或 de-escalation therapy\n         i. 縮短 therapy duration。\n         ii. 停用不必要的 antimicrobials。\n      d. Dose optimization\n         i. 應用 PK／PD principles。IDSA 特別建議對 vancomycin 與 aminoglycosides 實施 PK 與 dose-monitoring programs。\n         ii. 依 organ function 調整 dose。\n         iii. Allergy detection 與 assessment，尤其適當時推廣 β-lactam skin testing。\n      e. Parenteral-to-oral conversion。\n      f. 近期 IDSA guidelines 不建議單靠 didactic education 進行 stewardship。\n   3. Microbiology laboratory、electronic medical record system surveillance 與 clinical decision support 的支援，可進一步增強 stewardship 工作。\nD. Antimicrobial Stewardship Strategies（可協同使用）\n   1. Prospective audit、intervention 與 feedback（「back-end」strategy）\n      a. 提供彈性，並盡量減少給藥延遲。\n      b. 最成功的策略包括直接與 treating physicians 溝通，並要求記錄接受建議，或拒絕的理由。\n   2. Formulary restriction 與 preauthorization（「front-end」strategy）\n      a. 可能需大量 resources，prescribers 也可能感覺失去 autonomy。\n      b. 透過 infectious disease experts 會診，可最佳化 initial antimicrobial choices。", "en": "5. In 2019, the CDC updated the hospital core elements to reflect the new evidence in the field of antimicrobial stewardship. Major updates include hospital leadership commitment, accountability, pharmacy expertise, tracking, reporting, and education.\n\nB. Antimicrobial Stewardship Definition: Multidisciplinary and coordinated interventions designed to improve and measure the appropriate use of antimicrobial agents and to promote the selection of optimal antimicrobial drug regimen, including dosing, duration, and route of administration.\n\n1. Core members of a multidisciplinary antimicrobial stewardship team should include an infectious diseases physician, a clinical pharmacist, a clinical microbiologist, an information systems specialist, an infection control professional, a nurse, and a hospital epidemiologist.\n\n2. Broad-spectrum antimicrobials are often necessary in the ICU to provide early effective therapy. However, continued use of broad-spectrum antimicrobials may lead to the selection of pathogenic organisms (i.e., C. difficile, Candida spp.), nephrotoxicity, and the emergence of resistance.\n\nC. Critical Care Pharmacists – Well positioned to provide guidance on antimicrobial therapy, including expedited selection of appropriate initial agents, aggressive dosing to optimize PD, interpretation of microbiological evidence, appropriate de-escalation of antimicrobials, monitoring of response and potential adverse effects, and determination of the appropriate treatment duration\n\n1. Critical care pharmacists could either have an active role as a member of a multidisciplinary antibiotic stewardship team or serve in many of the different roles and activities of antibiotic stewardship.\n\n2. Core activities that can be pursued through formal pathways or everyday clinical interventions:\n\na. Education with active intervention – Interpretation of rapid identification tests and susceptibility testing\n\nb. Guidelines and clinical pathway development. Recent IDSA guidelines recommend facilityspecific clinical practice guidelines or algorithms as an effective way of standardizing prescribing practices.\n\nc. Streamlining or de-escalation of therapy\n\ni. Shortening therapy duration ii. Discontinuing unnecessary antimicrobials\n\nd. Dose optimization\n\ni. Application of pharmacokinetic (PK)/PD principles. Per IDSA recommendations, PK and dosemonitoring programs are specifically recommended for vancomycin and aminoglycosides. ii. Dose adjustments based on organ function iii. Allergy detection and assessment, in particular promotion of β-lactam skin testing when appropriate\n\ne. Parenteral to oral conversion\n\nf. Recent IDSA guidelines recommend against the use of didactic education alone for stewardship.\n\n3. Support from microbiology laboratory and electronic medical record system surveillance and clinical decision support may further enhance stewardship efforts.\n\nD. Antimicrobial Stewardship Strategies (can be used synergistically)\n\n1. Prospective audit with intervention and feedback (“back-end” strategy)\n\na. Allows flexibility and minimizes delay in administering therapy\n\nb. The most successful strategy involves direct communication with treating physicians and required documentation for acceptance of recommendation or rationale for denial.\n\n2. Formulary restriction and preauthorization (“front-end” strategy).\n\na. May be resource-intensive, and prescribers may feel a loss of autonomy\n\nb. Initial choices of antimicrobials may be optimized through consultation with infectious disease experts."}, {"page": 19, "zh": "c. Antimicrobial cycling：formulary restriction 的一例，按排定時間移除並替換特定 antimicrobial 或 class，目的是降低 antimicrobial selection pressures。目前證據不足以支持 cycling strategies 有效。IDSA stewardship guidelines 不建議以 cycling 作為 stewardship strategy。有報告指出，限制一類 antibiotics 時，會造成另一類 antibiotics 的補償性過度使用。\n   3. 無論使用何種 strategies，或 clinical pathways 品質如何，programmatic antibiotic stewardship 都不能取代 clinical judgment。\n   4. 應使用 process indicators（如 days of therapy、provider 對 clinical pathway 的遵循、time to effective therapy）與 outcome measures（如 LOS、mortality、30-day readmission），評估 program success。\nE. 有效 Antimicrobial Stewardship Programs 可在財務上自給自足\n   1. Antimicrobials 最多占 hospital pharmacy budgets 的 30%，最多 50% 的 antimicrobial use 不適當，導致 cost 增加、resistant pathogens selection 增加，以及 OIs selection 增加。\n   2. 數項研究顯示，stewardship programs 與顯著 cost savings 有關。但多數只著重 antimicrobial costs，少有關注 indirect costs 與 implementation costs。\n   3. 目前有一項 proposed CMS rule，擬將 antibiotic prescribing patterns 納入 quality-reporting metrics。許多 CMS quality metrics 與 reimbursement 連結；若此 metric 也與 reimbursement 連結，將進一步增加實施 stewardship programs 的誘因。〔「目前」依 2024 教材原文。〕\n   4. Joint Commission 宣布自 2017 年 1 月起，實施針對 antimicrobial stewardship 的新 medication management standard。許多 standards 與 critical care pharmacists 相關：staff continuing education、patient 與 family education、參與 stewardship team，以及制定與執行 antimicrobial management protocols。\nF. 支持重症病人 Antimicrobial Stewardship 的證據\n   1. 此領域研究受限於 poor study design；但多數研究報告 overall antibiotics 或特定 antibiotic class 使用減少。有些也報告主要 resistance rates 降低。\n   2. 研究使用的 strategies 差異很大，包括 restriction、正式 infectious disease physician consultation、de-escalation protocols、computer-assisted decision support，以及 stewardship team 正式重新評估 empiric antibiotics。\n   3. 對接受 antibiotics 的 ICU 病人進行 prospective audit 與 feedback 的 before-after studies，其 meta-analyses 未發現 mortality 增加，顯示可安全應用於重症病人。", "en": "c. Antimicrobial cycling: An example of formulary restriction in which there is a scheduled removal and substitution of a specific antimicrobial or an antimicrobial class. It is an effort to minimize antimicrobial selection pressures. Evidence is insufficient to suggest that antimicrobial cycling strategies are effective. IDSA stewardship guidelines recommend against the use of antimicrobial cycling as a stewardship strategy. The compensatory overuse of another class of antibiotics has been reported when attempts to restrict a different class of antibiotics were implemented.\n\n3. Regardless of the strategies used or the quality of clinical pathways, programmatic antibiotic stewardship is not a substitute for clinical judgment.\n\n4. Process indicators (e.g., days of therapy, provider adherence to clinical pathway, time to effective therapy) and outcome measures (e.g., length of stay, mortality, 30-day readmission) should be used to gauge program success.\n\nE. Effective Antimicrobial Stewardship Programs Can Be Financially Self-Supporting\n\n1. Antimicrobials can account for up to 30% of hospital pharmacy budgets, with up to 50% of antimicrobial use being inappropriate, leading to increased cost, increased selection of resistant pathogens, and increased selection of opportunistic infections (OIs).\n\n2. Several studies have shown significant cost savings associated with antimicrobial stewardship programs. However, most of these studies focused only on antimicrobial costs, with little focus devoted to indirect costs and implementation costs.\n\n3. There is currently a proposed CMS rule for incorporating antibiotic prescribing patterns as one of the quality-reporting metrics. Many CMS quality metrics are tied to reimbursement. If this metric becomes tied to reimbursement, there will be further incentives to implement antimicrobial stewardship programs.\n\n4. Effective January 2017, the Joint Commission announced a new medication management standard that addresses antimicrobial stewardship. Many of the standards are applicable and relevant to critical care pharmacists: continuing education of staff, education of patients and family members, participation in an antimicrobial stewardship team, and development and execution of antimicrobial management protocols.\n\nF. Evidence Supporting Antimicrobial Stewardship Efforts in Critically Ill Patients\n\n1. Studies in this area have been limited by poor study design. However, most studies have reported a decreased use in either antibiotics overall or a targeted class of antibiotics. Some studies have also reported a decrease in key resistance rates.\n\n2. Antimicrobial stewardship strategies used in the studies have varied widely, including restriction, formal infectious disease physician consultation, protocols for de-escalation, implementation of computerassisted decision support, and formal reassessments of the empiric antibiotics by a stewardship team.\n\n3. Meta-analyses of before-after studies evaluating prospective audit and feedback to ICU patients receiving antibiotics found no increase in mortality, suggesting that this practice could safely be implemented in critically ill patients."}, {"page": 20, "zh": "## IV. RAPID DIAGNOSTIC TESTS\nA. 理由\n   1. Septic shock 病人適當 antimicrobials administration 延遲，與 survival 降低有關。\n   2. Severe infections 通常使用 broad-spectrum antimicrobials，以涵蓋所有可能 pathogens。\n   3. Rapid diagnostic tests 可協助 de-escalation，以落實 stewardship。Critical care pharmacists 提倡依 rapid diagnostic test results 適當使用 antimicrobials。\n   4. 許多情況中，若 stewardship 使 antibiotic consumption 減少，實施 rapid diagnostic tests 可達 cost neutral，甚至 cost savings。\n   5. IDSA stewardship guidelines 建議與 stewardship team 合併使用，以最佳化 antibiotic therapy 並改善 clinical outcomes。\n   6. Society of Infectious Diseases Pharmacists 的正式 position statement 表示，rapid diagnostic tests 可幫助 stewardship programs 減少不必要 exposure，並最佳化 patient care。\nB. 從 Positive Bloodstream Cultures 早期辨識 Pathogens\n   1. 下述方法都試圖縮短從 blood culture positivity 到 species identification 或 susceptibility testing 的時間。傳統方法可能需 72–96 小時。Early identification techniques 尋求在 culture positivity 後 24 小時內，提供可作為 clinical action 依據的資訊。Rapid diagnostic tests、targets 與 turnaround times 的例子見 Table 5。\n   2. 在相關研究中，多數 techniques 結合 stewardship，可顯著降低 health care costs 並改善 clinical outcomes。但許多是 single-center studies，external validity 因此有疑慮。單一機構導入 rapid diagnostic tests 的整體影響，取決於：\n      a. Targeted organisms 的 epidemiology。\n      b. 既有 stewardship teams 的存在與行動。\n      c. 目前 clinician prescribing patterns。\n      d. Patient population。\n   3. 大多數 techniques 的共同限制，是無法偵測 polymicrobial infections。\n   4. 已開發使用 whole blood（相較 blood culture medium 或 agar plates）的新方法：LightCycler SeptiFast、SepsiTest。\n      a. 使用 whole blood 的好處，是可在近期或目前接受 antibiotics 的病人辨識 bacteria。\n   5. 某些技術也已開發用於 respiratory cultures，但其 clinical adaptation 遠少於 blood cultures。\n   6. 可偵測 resistance mechanisms genetic encoding 的 rapid diagnostic tests，需更多 education 與 guidelines，協助 clinicians 選擇正確 therapy，因為無傳統 susceptibility results。依 resistance genes 與 species detection 採取的合理 approach 見 Table 6。\n   7. PNA fluorescence in situ hybridization（FISH）\n      a. Mechanism：針對 positive blood cultures 的 species-specific ribosomal RNA。\n      b. Sensitivity 與 specificity：96%–100%。", "en": "IV. RAPID DIAGNOSTIC TESTS\n\nA. Rationale\n\n1. There is an association between delay in administration of appropriate antimicrobials and decreased survival among patients with septic shock.\n\n2. Broad-spectrum antimicrobials are usually used in severe infections to ensure that all potential pathogens are covered.\n\n3. Rapid diagnostic tests may assist in de-escalation efforts in an attempt to practice antimicrobial stewardship. Critical care pharmacists are advocates for the appropriate use of antimicrobials according to the results of rapid diagnostic tests.\n\n4. In many cases, the implementation of rapid diagnostic tests may be cost neutral, or even constitute a cost savings, when antimicrobial stewardship efforts leading to decreased consumption of antibiotics occur.\n\n5. Recommended by IDSA antimicrobial stewardship guidelines to be used in combination with stewardship team to optimize antibiotic therapy and improve clinical outcomes\n\n6. The Society of Infectious Diseases Pharmacists released an official position statement stating that rapid diagnostic tests can help antimicrobial stewardship programs decrease unnecessary exposure and optimize patient care.\n\nB. Early Pathogen Identification from Positive Bloodstream Cultures\n\n1. All discussed methods attempt to shorten the time from blood culture positivity to species identification or susceptibility testing. Traditional pathogen identification and susceptibility testing can take 72–96 hours. Early pathogen identification techniques seek to provide clinically actionable information within the first 24 hours from the time of culture positivity. See Table 5 for examples of rapid diagnostic tests, corresponding targets, and respective turnaround times.\n\n2. Most of these techniques, when combined with antibiotic stewardship efforts, lead to significant reductions in health care costs and improvements in clinical outcomes in relevant studies. However, many of these were single-center studies, which makes external validity questionable. The overall impact of the implementation of rapid diagnostic tests in a single institution is determined by several factors.\n\na. Epidemiology of targeted organisms\n\nb. Presence and actions of existing antimicrobial stewardship teams\n\nc. Current clinician prescribing patterns\n\nd. Patient population\n\n3. The inability to detect polymicrobial infections is a common limitation to most of the techniques described.\n\n4. Newer methods using whole blood (vs. blood culture medium or agar plates) have been developed (LightCycler SeptiFast, SepsiTest).\n\na. A benefit to identification from whole blood is the ability to identify bacteria in patients with recent or current antibiotic exposure.\n\n5. Some of the technology discussed has been developed for respiratory cultures, but the clinical adaptation in that arena is considerably less than that for blood cultures.\n\n6. Application of rapid diagnostic tests that detect genetic encoding of resistance mechanisms requires further education and guidelines to assist clinicians in choosing the proper therapy because traditional susceptibility results are not available. See Table 6 for a reasonable approach based on the detection of resistance genes and species.\n\n7. Peptide nucleic acid (PNA) fluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH)\n\na. Mechanism: Targets species-specific ribosomal RNA from positive blood cultures\n\nb. Sensitivity and specificity: 96%–100%"}, {"page": 21, "zh": "c. 限制：不提供 antimicrobial sensitivity data。目前 FISH products 僅用於 species identification；但 FDA 已核准可偵測 mecA gene、辨識 methicillin resistance 的新產品，尚未 commercially available。\n      d. 應用\n         i. 區分 S. aureus 與可能 skin flora contamination 的 CoNS。\n         ii. 區分 Enterococcus faecium（常對 ampicillin、vancomycin resistant）與 Enterococcus faecalis。\n         iii. 對 empiric echinocandins 治療者，辨識 fluconazole-sensitive Candida spp.。\n         iv. 對 combination gram-negative therapy 治療者，區分 Pseudomonas 與 non-Pseudomonas gram-negative spp.。\n      e. 研究\n         i. 一項 retrospective study 評估以 PNA FISH 早期區分 CoNS 與 S. aureus bacteremia 的 outcome 與 economic benefit，顯示顯著 cost savings 與 median LOS 降低。需注意，PNA FISH results 結合 antimicrobial therapy team 的工作。對 Enterococcus spp.、Candida spp. 等其他 pathogens，也有類似結果。相反地，另一研究評估未使用 stewardship team 的 staphylococci PNA FISH 導入前後結果，未發現 patient LOS 或 vancomycin use 顯著影響。這顯示 rapid identification tests 可能只有結合 education 與 prospective alerts，通知 clinicians 結果的 clinical applicability，才有益處。\n         ii. 一項 prospective randomized controlled study，將病人分配為 CoNS／S. aureus PNA FISH results 在 3 小時內 early notification，或 usual care；intervention 與 mortality、antibiotic use 及 LOS 降低有關。最明顯的益處出現在重症病人。\n   8. Mass spectroscopy：MALDI-TOF\n      a. Mechanism：將 mass spectroscopy 與 library standards 比較，以辨識 pathogen species 及／或 resistance mechanisms。這是一種將 samples ionize、產生 mass spectrogram 的 analytic technique。每個 sample 的 spectrogram 如指紋般獨特，可與 reference standards library 配對辨識。\n      b. Sensitivity 與 specificity：98%–100%。\n      c. 限制\n         i. 與 PNA FISH 類似，不回報 antimicrobial susceptibility；但技術可偵測 resistance genes。用於 resistance genes 的 MALDI-TOF 目前尚未 commercially available。\n         ii. 不能用於 polymicrobial cultures。\n         iii. Unusual organisms 尚無 library，但 pathogen libraries 持續更新。\n      d. 應用：可早期辨識更多 pathogens，clinical applicability 可能比受限於特定 pathogen tests 的 PNA FISH 更廣。不同 pathogens 的 library standards 持續增加。", "en": "c. Limitations: Does not provide antimicrobial sensitivity data. Currently available FISH products are only used for species identification; however, the FDA approved a new product that could detect the mecA gene for detecting the presence of methicillin resistance. This product is not currently commercially available.\n\nd. Application\n\ni. Separates S. aureus from possible skin flora contamination of coagulase-negative staphylococci (CoNS). ii. Differentiates Enterococcus faecium (which is often resistant to ampicillin and vancomycin) from Enterococcus faecalis. iii. Identifies fluconazole-sensitive Candida spp. for patients empirically treated with echinocandins. iv. Detects Pseudomonas versus non-Pseudomonas gram-negative spp. in patients treated with combination gram-negative therapy.\n\ne. Studies\n\ni. A retrospective study evaluating the outcome and economic benefit of PNA FISH methods for the early differentiation of CoNS and S. aureus bacteremia in clinical practice showed a significant cost savings and a decrease in median LOS. Of note, the PNA FISH results were combined with the efforts of an antimicrobial therapy team. Similar results have been shown with PNA FISH implementations for other pathogens, including Enterococcus spp. and Candida spp. These results are in contrast to those of another study that evaluated the preand post-staphylococci PNA FISH implementation results without the use of an antimicrobial stewardship team. This study found no significant effects on patient LOS or vancomycin use. This suggests that rapid identification tests are probably beneficial only when combined with educational efforts and prospective alerts to notify clinicians of the clinical applicability of the test results. ii. In a prospective randomized controlled study in which patients were randomized to early notification of PNA FISH results for CoNS or S. aureus within 3 hours or usual care, intervention was associated with decreased mortality, decreased antibiotic use, and decreased LOS. The most pronounced benefits occurred in critically ill patients.\n\n8. Mass spectroscopy: Matrix-assisted laser desorption-ionization/time of flight (MALDI-TOF)\n\na. Mechanism: Mass spectroscopy is compared with library standards for identifying pathogen species and/or resistance mechanisms. Mass spectroscopy is an analytic technique whereby samples are ionized that produces a mass spectrogram for the sample. Each sample has a unique mass spectrogram, similar to a fingerprint, which can be matched to a library of reference standards for identification.\n\nb. Sensitivity and specificity: 98%–100%\n\nc. Limitations\n\ni. Similar to PNA FISH, no antimicrobial susceptibility is reported; however, the technology could detect genes encoding resistance. MALDI-TOF for resistance genes is currently not commercially available. ii. Cannot be used for polymicrobial cultures iii. No library is available for unusual organisms, though pathogen libraries are consistently being updated.\n\nd. Application: Potentially wider clinical applicability than PNA FISH (which is limited by the availability of specific tests for certain pathogens) with early identification of many more pathogens. Additional library standards for different pathogens are continually being added."}, {"page": 22, "zh": "e. 研究：數項研究已評估此策略。一項 MALDI-TOF 導入前後研究，顯示 time to pathogen identification 縮短，LOS、recurrent infections 與 mortality 降低。需注意，導入時包括 stewardship team 向 treating clinicians 傳達結果，並提供 evidence-based antibiotic recommendations。\n   9. PCR-based detection systems\n      a. MRSA PCR test\n         i. Mechanism：針對 mecA gene 的新型 multiplex real-time assay。\n         ii. Sensitivity 與 specificity：MRSA／MSSA identification 分別為 85% 與 92%。\n         iii. 應用：較早 de-escalate anti-MRSA antimicrobials，並較早對 MSSA 適當使用 antistaphylococcal penicillin（oxacillin、nafcillin、cefazolin）。\n            (a) 最多經驗與證據來自 pneumonia 病人 MRSA-active antibiotics 的 de-escalation。新證據也顯示，可用於 intra-abdominal infections、bloodstream infections、wound cultures 與 urinary cultures 的 de-escalation。\n            (b) Providers 可使用距採檢最長 14 天的 MRSA PCR results；一項研究第 14 天的 NPV 為 95.5%。另一研究顯示，ICU admission 前後 60 天內的 MRSA nares screening，有高 NPV（98%）與 specificity（96%）。〔時間方向請對照原文 within 60 days of ICU admission。〕\n         iv. 研究：一項 before-and-after study 顯示，導入 MRSA PCR test 可縮短 time to appropriate therapy，以及不必要 MRSA coverage 的 duration。Mean hospital costs 也下降，LOS 有下降趨勢。非常類似的另一研究將 test 與 stewardship 結合，LOS 與 cost 顯著下降，mortality 呈下降趨勢（18% vs. 26%）。\n      b. FilmArray System\n         i. Mechanism：multiplex PCR technology 辨識 bacterial species 與 resistance genes。\n         ii. Sensitivity 與 specificity\n            (a) Species identification：>90%。\n            (b) Resistance genes：100%；目前僅能偵測 mecA（methicillin resistance）、vanA/B（vancomycin resistance）、KPC（carbapenem resistance）。\n         iii. 應用：較早 escalation 或 de-escalation antimicrobial agents。\n         iv. 研究顯示 time to pathogen identification 與 antibiotic de-escalation 較早。一研究將 multiplex PCR 與 stewardship 結合，未發現 mortality、LOS 或 cost 差異。\n   10. Nanoparticles（Microarray）：Verigene blood culture test\n      a. Mechanism\n         i. 使用 nanoparticle technology，直接從 positive blood culture medium 偵測。\n         ii. Nucleic acid extraction 與 array hybridization。\n      b. 可偵測 resistance genes 的 commercially available products 中，發展最成熟者。\n      c. Sensitivity 與 specificity：93%–100%。\n      d. 研究：目前多數限於 in vitro evaluations，顯示 accuracy 高，並縮短 pathogen 與 resistance mechanism identification 時間。Clinical evidence 有限；但兩項小型 single-center studies 評估 Nanosphere technology 輔助 clinical decisions，顯示 time to appropriate antimicrobials、LOS 與 overall cost 降低。", "en": "e. Studies: This strategy has been evaluated in several studies. In a before-and-after study of MALDITOF implementation, a shortened time to pathogen identification and a decrease in LOS, recurrent infections, and mortality were seen. Of note, the implementation of MALDI-TOF included communicating the results to the treating clinicians by an antimicrobial stewardship team with evidence-based antibiotic recommendations.\n\n9. Polymerase chain reaction (PCR)-based detection systems\n\na. MRSA PCR test\n\ni. Mechanism: Novel multiplex real-time assay for mecA gene ii. Sensitivity and specificity: 85% and 92%, respectively, for MRSA and methicillin-susceptible\n\nS. aureus (MSSA) identification iii. Application: Earlier de-escalation of anti-MRSA antimicrobials and earlier appropriate treatment with antistaphylococcal penicillin (oxacillin, nafcillin, cefazolin) for MSSA\n\n(a) Most experience and evidence with using the MRSA PCR test is for de-escalation of MRSA-active antibiotics in patients with pneumonia. New evidence also shows this may be used for de-escalation in patients with intra-abdominal infections, bloodstream infections, wound cultures, and urinary cultures.\n\n(b) Providers may use results from MRSA PCR test for up to 14 days between specimen collections (negative predictive value at 14 days in one study was 95.5%). Another study demonstrated that MRSA nares screening within 60 days of ICU admission has a high negative predictive value (98%) and specificity (96%). iv. Studies: In a before-and-after study, implementation of the MRSA PCR test resulted in reduced time to appropriate therapy and duration of unnecessary MRSA coverage. In addition, the mean hospital costs were decreased, and there was a trend toward decreased LOS. In a very similar study, the combination of the MRSA PCR test with antimicrobial stewardship efforts resulted in significant decreases in LOS and cost and a trend toward decreased mortality (18% vs. 26%).\n\nb. FilmArray System\n\ni. Mechanism: Uses multiplex PCR technology to identify bacterial species and resistance genes ii. Sensitivity and specificity\n\n(a) For species identification: Greater than 90%\n\n(b) For resistance genes: 100% (currently only available for mecA - methicillin resistance; van A/B - vancomycin resistance; Klebsiella pneumoniae carbapenemase [KPC] - carbapenem resistance) iii. Application: Earlier escalation or de-escalation of antimicrobial agents iv. Studies have shown an earlier time to pathogen identification and antibiotic de-escalation. One study found no difference in mortality, LOS, or cost when multiplex PCR was combined with antimicrobial stewardship.\n\n10. Nanoparticles (Microarray): Verigene blood culture test\n\na. Mechanism\n\ni. Direct detection from positive blood culture medium using nanoparticle technology ii. Nucleic acid extraction and array hybridization\n\nb. Most-developed commercially available product with resistance gene detection\n\nc. Sensitivity and specificity: 93%–100%\n\nd. Studies: Currently, most studies are limited to in vitro evaluations, which showed high levels of accuracy and decreased time to pathogen and resistance mechanism identification. Limited clinical evidence; however, two small single-center studies have evaluated the use of Nanosphere technology to augment clinical decisions. These studies showed a decrease in time to appropriate antimicrobials, in addition to decreased LOS and overall cost."}, {"page": 23, "zh": "11. Chromogenic media\n      a. Mechanism\n         i. 利用顏色產生，辨識不同 microorganisms 的 microbiological media。\n         ii. Growth media 使用 hydrolysis 時釋出 colored dyes 的 enzyme substrates，可針對廣泛 enzymes。\n         iii. 可能優點是能偵測 polymicrobial growth。\n      b. Sensitivity 與 specificity：95%–100%。\n      c. 限制\n         i. 不同公司製造不同 chromogenic agar media，如 Brilliance、chromID、CHROMagar。研究中的 sensitivity 與 specificity 略有差異，但均在可接受範圍。\n         ii. Time to identification 比其他 rapid diagnostic tests 長。\n         iii. 不同廠商 agar 的 positive identification 顏色不同。判讀者應充分受訓，熟悉當地機構使用的產品。\n      d. 應用\n         i. 從其他 Staphylococcus spp. 分離 S. aureus。\n         ii. 偵測 S. aureus 的 methicillin resistance。\n         iii. 偵測 vancomycin resistance。\n         iv. 偵測特定 Enterobacterales：Salmonella、E. coli O157，以及 ESBL production。\n         v. 區分不同 Candida spp.。\n         vi. 偵測 KPC。\n      e. 研究：許多 clinical studies 顯示，比 conventional culture media 有顯著優勢。隨新技術與更短 detection times 出現，其 clinical applicability 可能受限。然而，因 considerable upfront costs，只有少數 microbiology laboratories 導入 rapid diagnostic methods；使用 chromogenic media 的 centers，可能持續依賴此技術。\n### Table 5. Positive Blood Cultures 的 Rapid Diagnostic Tests 例子與特性\n|Assay technology|Manufacturer／trade name|Organisms／antimicrobial resistance targets|Blood culture positive growth 後 detection time|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|PNA FISH|AdvanDx／PNA FISH、Traffic Light；AdvanDx／QuickFISH|S. aureus、CoNS、E. faecalis、E. faecium、E. coli、K. pneumoniae、P. aeruginosa、C. albicans、C. glabrata、C. parapsilosis、C. tropicalis、C. krusei|PNA FISH 1.5 hr；QuickFISH 20 min（目前未經 FDA 核准用於 Candida spp.）|\n|PCR|BD GeneOhm／Staph SR；Cepheid／Xpert MRSA|S. aureus、CoNS／mecA（methicillin）|1–2 hr|", "en": "11. Chromogenic media\n\na. Mechanism\n\ni. Microbiological media used to identify different microorganisms by color production ii. Growth media use enzyme substrates that release colored dyes on hydrolysis, with a wide range of enzymes that can be targeted iii. Potential advantage of being able to detect polymicrobial growth\n\nb. Sensitivity and specificity: 95%–100%\n\nc. Limitations\n\ni. Many different companies make different chromogenic agar media (Brilliance, chromID, CHROMagar). Slight differences in sensitivity and specificity were seen in studies; however, all were within acceptable ranges. ii. Time to identification is longer than with other rapid diagnostic tests. iii. Different manufacturers’ chromogenic agar produces different colors for positive identification. Readers of chromogenic agar should be sufficiently trained and familiar with the product used by the local institution.\n\nd. Application\n\ni. Isolation of S. aureus from other Staphylococcus spp. ii. Detection of methicillin resistance among S. aureus iii. Detection of vancomycin resistance iv. Detection of specific Enterobacterales: Salmonella, E. coli O157, extended-spectrum β-lactamase (ESBL) production\n\nv. Differentiation of different Candida spp. vi. Detection of KPC\n\ne. Studies: Many clinical studies have shown significant advantages over conventional culture media. With the advent of newer technology and shorter detection times, the clinical applicability of chromogenic media may be limited. However, few microbiology laboratories have implemented rapid diagnostic methods because of the considerable upfront costs. Centers where chromogenic media are being used may continue to rely on this technology.\n\nTable 5. Examples of Rapid Diagnostic Tests of Positive Blood Cultures and Their Characteristics Assay Technology Manufacturer/ Trade Name Organisms/Antimicrobial Resistance Targets Detection Time After Positive Growth on Blood Culture PNA FISH • AdvanDx/PNA FISH, Traffic Light • AdvanDx/ QuickFISH\n\nS. aureus, CoNS, E. faecalis, E. faecium, E. coli,\n\nK. pneumoniae, P. aeruginosa, C. albicans,\n\nC. glabrata, C. parapsilosis, C. tropicalis,\n\nC. krusei 1.5 hr – PNA FISH 20 min – QuickFISH – Not currently FDA approved for Candida spp. PCR • BD GeneOhm/ Staph SR • Cepheid/Xpert MRSA\n\nS. aureus, CoNS/mecA (methicillin) 1–2 hr"}, {"page": 24, "zh": "### Table 5. Positive Blood Cultures 的 Rapid Diagnostic Tests 例子與特性 a（續）\n|Assay technology|Manufacturer／trade name|Organisms／antimicrobial resistance targets|Detection time|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|PCR|BioFire／FilmArray|Enterococcus spp.、L. monocytogenes、S. aureus、S. agalactiae、S. pneumoniae、S. pyogenes／mecA（methicillin）、vanA/B（vancomycin）；A. baumannii、H. influenzae、N. meningitidis、P. aeruginosa、E. cloacae、E. coli、K. oxytoca、K. pneumoniae、Proteus spp.、S. marcescens／KPC（carbapenem）；C. albicans、C. glabrata、C. krusei、C. parapsilosis、C. tropicalis|1 hr，直接從 blood culture media|\n|MALDI-TOF|BioMérieux／Vitek MS；Bruker／Microflex|多種 pathogens，包括 bacteria、yeast、mold、mycobacteria；resistance mechanisms 偵測仍在開發|10–30 min|\n|Nanoparticles（Microarray）|Nanosphere／Verigene|S. aureus、S. epidermidis、S. lugdunensis、S. anginosus、S. agalactiae、S. pneumoniae、S. pyogenes、E. faecalis、E. faecium、Staphylococcus spp.、Streptococcus spp.、Micrococcus spp.、Listeria spp.／mecA（methicillin）、vanA（vancomycin）、vanB（vancomycin）；E. coli、K. pneumoniae、K. oxytoca、P. aeruginosa、S. marcescens、Acinetobacter spp.、Citrobacter spp.、Enterobacter spp.、Proteus spp.／CTX-M（ESBL）、IMP、KPC、NDM、OXA、VIM（carbapenemase）；Candida spp. 偵測仍在開發|2 hr，直接從 blood culture media|\n|Chromogenic media|CHROMagar|S. aureus、MRSA、Enterococcus spp.、VRE、S. agalactiae、E. coli（Shiga toxin、EC-O157）、Klebsiella spp.、Proteus spp.、Pseudomonas spp.、Acinetobacter spp.、Yersinia spp.；KPC（carbapenem）、CTX-M（ESBL）；C. albicans、C. tropicalis、C. krusei|24–48 hr|\nESBL = extended-spectrum β-lactamase；KPC = Klebsiella pneumoniae carbapenemase；MALDI-TOF = matrix-assisted laser desorption-ionization/time of flight；MRSA = methicillin-resistant S. aureus；NDM = New Delhi metallo-β-lactamase；PCR = polymerase chain reaction；PNA FISH = peptide nucleic acid fluorescence in situ hybridization；VRE = vancomycin-resistant enterococci。\n原教材經授權重製自：Goff DA, Jankowski C, Tenover F. Using rapid diagnostic tests to optimize antimicrobial selection in antimicrobial stewardship programs. Pharmacotherapy 2012;32:677-87。", "en": "Assay Technology Manufacturer/ Trade Name Organisms/Antimicrobial Resistance Targets Detection Time After Positive Growth on Blood Culture PCR • BioFire/ FilmArray Enterococcus spp., L. monocytogenes\n\nS. aureus, S. agalactiae, S. pneumoniae,\n\nS. pyogenes/mecA (methicillin), vanA/B (vancomycin)\n\nA. baumannii, H. inÞuenzae, N. meningitidis,\n\nP. aeruginosa, E. cloacae, E. coli, K. oxytoca,\n\nK. pneumoniae, Proteus spp., S. marcescens/KPC (carbapenem)\n\nC. albicans, C. glabrata, C. krusei,\n\nC. parapsilosis, C. tropicalis 1 hr – Direct from blood culture media MALDI-TOF • BioMérieux/ Vitek MS • Bruker/ Microflex Several pathogens, including bacteria, yeast, mold, mycobacteria/resistance mechanisms are in development 10–30 min Nanoparticles (Microarray) • Nanosphere/ Verigene\n\nS. aureus, S. epidermidis, S. lugdunensis,\n\nS. anginosus, S. agalactiae, S. pneumoniae,\n\nS. pyogenes, E. faecalis, E. faecium, Staphylococcus spp., Streptococcus spp., Micrococcus spp., Listeria spp./mecA (methicillin), vanA (vancomycin), vanB (vancomycin)\n\nE. coli, K. pneumoniae, K. oxytoca,\n\nP. aeruginosa, S. marcescens, Acinetobacter spp., Citrobacter spp., Enterobacter spp., Proteus spp./ CTX-M (ESBL), IMP (carbapenemase), KPC (carbapenemase), NDM (carbapenemase), OXA (carbapenemase), VIM (carbapenemase) Candida spp. in development 2 hr – Direct from blood culture media Chromogenic media • CHROMagar\n\nS. aureus, MRSA, Enterococcus spp.,VRE,\n\nS. agalactiae, E. coli (Shiga toxin, EC-O157), Klebsiella spp., Proteus spp., Pseudomonas spp., Acinetobacter spp., Yersinia spp.; KPC (carbapenem), CTX-M (ESBL)\n\nC. albicans, C. tropicalis, C. krusei 24–48 hr ESBL = extended-spectrum β-lactamase; KPC = Klebsiella pneumoniae carbapenemase; MALDI-TOF = matrix-assisted laser desorption-ionization/time of flight; MRSA = methicillin-resistant S. aureus; NDM = New Delhi metallo-β-lactamase; PCR = polymerase chain reaction; PNA FISH = peptide nucleic acid fluorescence in situ hybridization; VRE = vancomycin-resistant enterococci. Reproduced with permission from: Goff DA, Jankowski C, Tenover F. Using rapid diagnostic tests to optimize antimicrobial selection in antimicrobial stewardship programs. Pharmacotherapy 2012;32:677-87.\n\nTable 5. Examples of Rapid Diagnostic Tests of Positive Blood Cultures and Their Characteristicsa (continued)"}, {"page": 25, "zh": "### Table 6. Positive Blood Cultures 的 Rapid Diagnostic Tests 偵測 Resistance-Encoding Genes 後，合理的 Empiric Treatment Approach a（原標題含 continued，保留）\n|Resistance genes|Species|建議 therapy|Alternative therapy|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|mecA-negative|S. aureus|Oxacillin、nafcillin、cefazolin|Vancomycin，若不耐受 β-lactams|\n|mecA-positive|S. aureus|Vancomycin|Daptomycin、linezolid、ceftaroline|\n|vanA/B-negative|E. faecalis|Ampicillin|Vancomycin，若 β-lactam allergy|\n|vanA/B-positive|E. faecalis|Daptomycin|Linezolid|\n|vanA/B-negative|E. faecium|Vancomycin|Daptomycin，若不耐受 vancomycin|\n|vanA/B-positive|E. faecium|Daptomycin|Linezolid|\n|CTX-M（ESBL）a|Enteric gram-negative pathogens|Carbapenems：ertapenem、imipenem、meropenem|Ceftazidime/avibactam|\n|KPC a|K. pneumoniae 與其他 enteric gram-negative pathogens|Ceftazidime/avibactam、meropenem/vaborbactam、imipenem/cilastatin/relebactam|Colistin/polymyxin B、tigecycline/eravacycline|\n|NDM carbapenemase a|K. pneumoniae 與其他 enteric gram-negative pathogens|Cefiderocol；aztreonam + ceftazidime/avibactam|Colistin/polymyxin B、tigecycline|\n|VIM 或 IMP carbapenemase a|P. aeruginosa|Colistin/polymyxin B、aztreonam、cefiderocol|—|\n|OXA β-lactamase a|P. aeruginosa 與 Enterobacterales|Colistin/polymyxin B、carbapenem b|Cefiderocol|\n|OXA β-lactamase a|A. baumannii|Minocycline、ceftazidime/avibactam、sulbactam/durlobactam|Cefiderocol、colistin/polymyxin B、tigecycline、eravacycline、carbapenem|\na. Gram-negative pathogens 的 resistance mechanisms 較複雜，常有多種機轉。因此建議 therapies 代表完整 susceptibility reports 前的合理 empiric approach；仍可調整為較廣或較窄 spectrum。\nb. OXA β-lactamase 存在時，carbapenem MIC 可能較高。若使用 carbapenem，可考慮 maximal doses。", "en": "Table 6. Reasonable Empiric Treatment Approach Associated with Detection of Antimicrobial Resistance Encoding Genes from Rapid Diagnostic Tests for Positive Blood Culturesa (continued) Resistance Genes Species Recommended Therapy Alternative Therapy mecA-negative S. aureus Oxacillin Nafcillin Cefazolin Vancomycin (if intolerance to β-lactams) mecA-positive S. aureus Vancomycin Daptomycin Linezolid Ceftaroline vanA/B-negative E. faecalis Ampicillin Vancomycin (if allergic to β-lactams) vanA/B-positive E. faecalis Daptomycin Linezolid vanA/B-negative E. faecium Vancomycin Daptomycin (if intolerance to vancomycin) vanA/B-positive E. faecium Daptomycin Linezolid CTX-M (ESBL)a Enteric gram-negative pathogens Carbapenems (ertapenem, imipenem, meropenem) Ceftazidime/avibactam KPCa\n\nK. pneumoniae and other enteric gram-negative pathogens Ceftazidime/avibactam Meropenem/vaborbactam Imipenem/cilastatin/ relebactam Colistin/polymyxin B Tigecycline/eravacycline NDM carbapenemasea\n\nK. pneumoniae and other enteric gram-negative pathogens Cefiderocol Aztreonam + ceftazidime/ avibactam Colistin/polymyxin B Tigecycline VIM or IMP carbapenemasea\n\nP. aeruginosa Colistin/polymyxin B Aztreonam Cefiderocol OXA β-lactamasea\n\nP. aeruginosa and Enterobacterales Colistin/polymyxin B Carbapenemb Cefiderocol OXA β-lactamasea A. baumannii Minocycline Ceftazidime/avibactam Sulbactam/durlobactam Cefiderocol Colistin/polymyxin B Tigecycline Eravacycline Carbapenem aResistance mechanisms associated with gram-negative pathogens are more complicated. Often, there is more than one resistance mechanism. Hence, the recommended therapies represent reasonable empiric approaches before full antimicrobial susceptibility reports. However, therapy may be tailored to either a broader or a narrower spectrum. bCarbapenem may have a higher MIC in the presence of OXA β-lactamase. If using carbapenem, may consider using maximal doses."}, {"page": 26, "zh": "## Patient Case\n3. 一名 54 歲男性因 acute necrotizing pancreatitis 入住 medical ICU。發現 infected pancreatic abscess，接受 meropenem 與 vancomycin。療程一週後出現 fever、leukocytosis、hemodynamically unstable 與 oliguria。Empiric caspofungin 用以涵蓋可能 invasive candidiasis。Blood cultures 轉 positive，初步結果為 yeast。機構具備 PNA FISH technology，治療第 2 天辨識為 Candida parapsilosis。病人仍 hemodynamically unstable。Antifungal therapy 最適當選擇為何？\n   A. 繼續 caspofungin，等待 fungal susceptibilities 完成。\n   B. 改為 voriconazole 6 mg/kg，每 12 小時一次。\n   C. 改為 liposomal amphotericin 5 mg/kg/day。\n   D. 改為 fluconazole 400 mg IV 每日一次。\nC. 早期 C. difficile Identification：Nucleic acid amplification methods（PCR、loop-mediated isothermal amplification）\n   1. Assays 針對 toxin A 或 toxin B gene 的 DNA sequence。\n   2. Turnaround time：1–3 小時。\n   3. Sensitivity 與 specificity：90%–96%。\n      a. Sensitivity 增加，可能使 false-positive rates 增加。\n      b. C. difficile prevalence 下降時，PPV 下降，可能造成不必要 overtreatment。\n      c. 應透過 education 避免過度開立 rapid nucleic acid amplification tests。也應避免 serial tests；此做法在使用 enzyme immunoassays 時很常見。因 sensitivity 已足夠高，serial ordering 只會進一步增加 false positivity 機率。\nD. 早期 Fungal Organisms Identification\n   1. 組織病理已證實 invasive candidiasis 的病人中，最多 50% blood cultures 為 negative。\n   2. Aspergillus cultures 缺乏 sensitivity，且可能需很長 growth time。\n   3. 重症病人通常無法進行 biopsies。\n   4. 需 fungal infection surrogate markers，供 early diagnosis，避免與較差 outcomes 相關的 treatment delay。\n   5. β-D-Glucan\n      a. 存在於多數 fungal pathogens 的 cell membrane，Mucor、Cryptococcus 除外。可能成為 Candida、Aspergillus 與 Pneumocystis screening tool。〔原文 cell membrane 依原文保留。〕\n      b. Fungitell assay 可偵測 serum β-D-glucan，2 小時內提供結果。\n      c. 文獻對 positive result 的 cutoff 不同。一項近期評估重症病人 prophylactic 與 preemptive antifungal therapy 的研究，以 >80 pg/mL 為建議 positive cutoff。\n      d. 不同 populations 的 sensitivity 與 specificity 差異很大。\n      e. 診斷 invasive fungal infections 時，研究一致顯示高 NPV、低 PPV，因此低值時最適合用於 screening-out。低 PPV 可能因許多 clinical scenarios 可造成 false positives：\n         i. 接觸含 β-D-glucan 的 surgical supplies 與 topical products。", "en": "Patient Case\n\n3. A 54-year-old man is admitted to the medical ICU with acute necrotizing pancreatitis. He is found to have an infected pancreatic abscess, which is being treated with meropenem and vancomycin. One week into the course, the patient develops a fever and leukocytosis. He also becomes hemodynamically unstable and oliguric. He is initiated on caspofungin empirically to cover for possible invasive candidiasis. Blood cultures are obtained, which become positive with a preliminary result of yeast. This institution is equipped with PNA FISH technology, which identifies the yeast as Candida parapsilosis on day 2 of therapy. The patient remains hemodynamically unstable. Which is the most appropriate choice for this patient’s antifungal therapy?\n\nA. Continue caspofungin while fungal susceptibilities are finalized.\n\nB. Change to voriconazole 6 mg/kg every 12 hours.\n\nC. Change to liposomal amphotericin 5 mg/kg/day.\n\nD. Change to fluconazole 400 mg intravenously daily.\n\nC. Early C. difficile Identification: Nucleic acid amplification methods (PCR and loop-mediated isothermal amplification)\n\n1. Assays are targeting DNA sequence for the toxin A or toxin B gene.\n\n2. Turnaround time: 1–3 hours\n\n3. Sensitivity and specificity: 90%–96%\n\na. Because of increased sensitivity, the false-positive rates may be increased.\n\nb. As the prevalence of C. difficile decreases, the positive predictive value decreases, which may lead to unnecessary overtreatment.\n\nc. Educational efforts should be made to discourage the practice of over-ordering C. difficile rapid nucleic acid amplification tests. In addition, clinicians should be discouraged from ordering serial tests, which was a common practice when enzyme immunoassays were used. Because the sensitivity is sufficiently high, serial ordering only furthers the chance of false positivity.\n\nD. Early Identification of Fungal Organisms\n\n1. Up to 50% of patients with histopathologically proven invasive candidiasis have negative blood cultures.\n\n2. Cultures for Aspergillus lack sensitivity and may require significant growth time.\n\n3. Biopsies are often not feasible in critically ill patients.\n\n4. Surrogate markers of fungal infections are needed for early diagnosis and to avoid delays in treatment, which have been associated with worsened outcomes.\n\n5. β-d-Glucan\n\na. Found in the cell membrane of most fungal pathogens (except for Mucor and Cryptococcus). Potentially a screening tool for Candida, Aspergillus, and Pneumocystis.\n\nb. Fungitell assay can detect β-d-glucan in serum and provide results within 2 hours.\n\nc. Variable cutoffs are described in the literature for a positive result. A suggested cutoff for positive results, as used in a recent study evaluating prophylactic and preemptive antifungal therapy in critically ill patients, is greater than 80 pg/mL.\n\nd. Considerable differences in sensitivity and specificity values have been seen in different populations.\n\ne. Consistently high negative predictive values and low positive predictive values have been seen for the diagnosis of invasive fungal infections, which suggests that it is best used as a screeningout tool when the values are low. Low positive predictive value may occur because many clinical scenarios could lead to false-positive results.\n\ni. Exposure to β-d-glucan–containing surgical supplies and topical products"}, {"page": 27, "zh": "ii. Candida colonization。\n         iii. Thrush 與 mucositis。\n         iv. Dialysis filters 的 cellulose membranes。\n         v. Bacterial infections。\n         vi. 接受 β-lactam antibiotics、albumin 或 immunoglobulins。\n      f. 若作為考慮啟動 treatment 的工具，連續兩次 tests positive 時效果最佳。\n      g. 此為非特異 fungal element，難以解讀；可能偵測 Aspergillus、Candida 與 Pneumocystis 的 elements，不能辨識不同 species。\n      h. 已與重症病人 invasive candidiasis 的 clinical prediction scores 結合評估，以啟動 empiric antifungal therapy。以 β-D-glucan 作 screening tool 時，empiric echinocandin therapy 與 placebo 相比，clinical outcomes 無顯著差異。\n   6. T2 magnetic resonance\n      a. Nanodiagnostic approach，偵測 amplified Candida DNA；類似傳統 MRI techniques，但在微小尺度上進行。\n      b. 對 whole blood 執行；magnetic particles 表面包覆可特異結合 Candida DNA 的 agents。\n      c. Whole blood 有 Candida 時，會與 particles 結合並聚集，造成 magnetic fields 的 microscopic disruptions。\n      d. 目前 FDA 核准 5 種 pathogenic Candida species：C. albicans、C. glabrata、C. parapsillosis、C. tropicalis、C. kruseii。〔Species 拼字依本段原文。〕\n      e. Sensitivity 高（91%）、specificity 高（98%），但缺乏 clinical study application。\n   7. Mannan／Anti-mannan\n      a. Mannan 是 fungal cell wall 的 polysaccharide component，對 Candida spp. 具特異性。\n      b. Mannan antigen 與因 mannan 產生的 anti-mannan antibodies，均有 commercially available latex agglutination 與 enzyme immunoassay。\n      c. 兩項 tests 比 β-D-glucan 更 specific，但 sensitivity 較低。\n      d. 納入 non-neutropenic 重症病人研究的 meta-analysis 顯示，合併兩項 tests 可改善 sensitivity 與 specificity。Sensitivity 也依 Candida spp. 而異，C. albicans 最高，C. parapsilosis 最低。\n   8. Galactomannan\n      a. Aspergillus spp. 的 cell wall component。\n      b. Platelia enzyme immunoassay 可在 4 小時內，偵測 serum 或其他 sterile fluids（bronchoalveolar lavage）的 galactomannan。\n      c. Sensitivity、specificity 不一；偵測 Aspergillus 時，hematologic malignancy 病人的 PPV、NPV 通常優於 SOT 族群。\n      d. 同時給予某些 β-lactam antibiotics（piperacillin/tazobactam、amoxicillin/clavulanic acid），或存在其他 invasive mycoses（Penicillium、histoplasmosis、blastomycosis），可造成 false positives。\n   9. PCR\n      a. 有 FDA-approved assay，但僅可偵測 Candida spp.。\n      b. 可 early detection candidemia。\n      c. Sensitivity 與 specificity 高，NPV 與 PPV 良好。\n      d. Colonization 可能降低 specificity；過早使用（如新 symptoms 出現前）可能降低 sensitivity。", "en": "ii. Colonization with Candida iii. Thrush and mucositis iv. Cellulose membranes from dialysis filters\n\nv. Bacterial infections vi. Receipt of β-lactam antibiotics, albumin, or immunoglobulins\n\nf. When used as a tool to potentially initiate treatment, optimal results occur when two consecutive tests are positive.\n\ng. Nonspecific fungal element makes interpretation difficult. May detect elements from Aspergillus, Candida, and Pneumocystis. Does not detect different species.\n\nh. Has been evaluated in combination with clinical prediction scores for invasive candidiasis in critically ill patients for initiating empiric antifungal therapy. When using β-d-glucan as a screening tool, empiric echinocandin therapy does not result in any significant differences in clinical outcomes compared with placebo.\n\n6. T2 magnetic resonance\n\na. Nanodiagnostic approach, which detects amplified Candida DNA. Similar to traditional MRI techniques, but done on a micro scale.\n\nb. Performed on whole blood, where magnetic particles that are coated with agents specific for binding to Candida DNA.\n\nc. When Candida is present in whole blood, it will bind to the particles and cluster, causing microscopic disruptions in the magnetic fields.\n\nd. Currently, FDA approved for 5 pathogenic Candida species (C. albicans, C. glabrata, C. parapsillosis, C. tropicalis, C. kruseii)\n\ne. High sensitivity (91%) and specificity (98%) but lacks clinical study application\n\n7. Mannan/Anti-mannan\n\na. Mannan is a polysaccharide component of the fungal cell wall that is specific to Candida spp.\n\nb. A commercially available latex agglutination and enzyme immunoassay exists for both mannan antigen and anti-mannan antibibodies that develop in response to mannan.\n\nc. Both tests are more specific than the β-d-glucan test, but they are not as sensitive.\n\nd. A meta-analysis that included studies in non-neutropenic critically ill patients found improved sensitivity and specificity of both tests when used in combination. It also demonstrated a varied sensitivity depending on the Candida spp (C. albicans with the highest and C. parapsilosis with the lowest).\n\n8. Galactomannan\n\na. Cell wall component of Aspergillus spp.\n\nb. Platelia enzyme immunoassay can detect galactomannan in serum or other sterile fluids (bronchoalveolar lavage) within 4 hours.\n\nc. Variable sensitivity and specificity, with generally better positive and negative predictive values for the detection of Aspergillus in the patient population with hematologic malignancies than in the solid organ transplant (SOT) population\n\nd. False positives can occur with the simultaneous administration of certain β-lactam antibiotics (piperacillin/tazobactam, amoxicillin/clavulanic acid) or the presence of other invasive mycoses (Penicillium, histoplasmosis, blastomycosis).\n\n9. PCR\n\na. An FDA-approved assay is available for detecting Candida spp. only.\n\nb. This test allows for the early detection of candidemia.\n\nc. This assay has high sensitivity and specificity and a good negative and positive predictive value.\n\nd. Colonization may decrease specificity and using the test too early (e.g., prior to onset of new symptoms) may decrease sensitivity."}, {"page": 28, "zh": "E. Procalcitonin（PCT）\n   1. 反映 host 對 bacterial infections response 的 inflammatory biomarker。\n   2. Bacterial toxins 與部分 bacterial proinflammatory mediators（如 IL-1b、IL-6、TNFα）會上調 PCT synthesis；對 viral infections 通常釋出的 cytokines（如 interferon-γ）則無此反應。平常 PCT concentrations 無法偵測（<0.05 mcg/L），但接觸 bacterial toxins 後，2–4 小時內快速釋出。Plasma half-life 為 24 小時。文獻中 infected patients 的 concentrations 差異很大；但感染期間較高 max concentration，似與較高 mortality incidence 相關。\n   3. PCT 有多種用途，包括 sepsis diagnosis 與 prognostication。IDSA stewardship guidelines 建議 serial measurements 結合其他 stewardship interventions，以降低 antibiotic use。Surviving Sepsis Campaign 提出 weak recommendation、low-quality evidence：對 sepsis 病人，若無 infection evidence，可用 low PCT 協助 clinicians 停用 empiric antibiotics。\n   4. 關於 antibiotic use 與 duration 的 clinical decisions，PCT 已被評估用於 initiation、cessation，以及兩者合併。這些 strategies 假定 institutional laboratory 能提供 PCT。若 turnaround time >24 小時，減少 antimicrobial treatment days 的效果可能有限。\n   5. 特定 populations 的 PCT interpretation 尚不明；但只要 providers 知道 limitations，並非不能使用。依目前證據，下列族群須審慎：\n      a. CKD：baseline PCT levels 較高。\n      b. Noninfectious conditions 也可使 PCT 升高，包括 trauma、surgery、burns、增加 proinflammatory cytokines 的 immunomodulator therapy、cardiogenic shock、peritoneal dialysis，以及 cirrhosis 病人。\n   6. 依目前證據，無 infection signs／symptoms 者，不應 routine 測 PCT。僅依 PCT 對無症狀者啟動 antibiotics，可能造成過度使用與相關 adverse effects。一項研究將 1200 名重症病人 randomize 至 PCT alert strategy 或 standard of care。Intervention group 的 PCT >1.0 mcg/L 會發出 alert，強制 clinical intervention，包括 microbiological cultures、追加 radiologic assessment，及／或啟動、擴大 antimicrobial coverage。整體未改善 mortality 或 time to appropriate antibiotics；反而 mechanical ventilation 需求增加，ICU LOS 與 antibiotic use 延長。\n   7. 有 infection signs／symptoms 的重症病人，不應以症狀發生時的 baseline PCT，決定是否啟動 antibiotics。這種情況因 low PCT withholding antibiotics 的 compliance rate 一直很低。實際 clinical practice 可能比 studies 更低，但尚未評估。若取得 baseline PCT，應用於觀察趨勢，考慮 early discontinuation。一項評估有 infection signs／symptoms 者，PCT-guided strategy 能否限制 antibiotic initiation 的研究，未發現 antibiotic use 差異；可能因 low PCT 時僅 36% clinicians 遵循 withholding 建議，與 high PCT 時 86% 遵循 initiation 建議形成強烈對比。\n   8. 有 infection signs／symptoms 的重症病人，應取得 baseline PCT 供趨勢觀察。Antibiotic treatment 期間 low PCT 或相較 baseline 大幅下降，應用於縮短 antimicrobial therapy duration；可藉停用未感染者不必要 antibiotics，或縮短感染者療程達成。此策略在廣泛重症病人中已證實安全有效。數項研究評估以 PCT guidance 決定適當 discontinuation 及／或 de-escalation 時間。", "en": "E. Procalcitonin (PCT)\n\n1. An inflammatory biomarker that reflects host response to bacterial infections\n\n2. PCT synthesis is up-regulated by bacterial toxins and certain bacterial proinflammatory mediators such as interleukin (IL)-1b, IL-6, and tumor necrosis factor alpha (TNFα), but it is neutral to cytokines that are normally released for viral infections such as interferon-γ. Usual concentrations of PCT are undetectable (less than 0.05 mcg/L). However, on exposure to bacterial toxins, PCT is rapidly released within 2–4 hours. The plasma half-life of PCT is 24 hours. Concentrations in the literature for infected patients vary greatly; however, it appears that a higher max concentration of PCT during infection correlates with a higher incidence of mortality.\n\n3. PCT is used in many roles, including the diagnosis and prognostication for sepsis. IDSA stewardship guidelines recommend serial measurements be used in conjunction with other stewardship interventions to decrease antibiotics use. The Surviving Sepsis Campaign provides a weak recommendation (weak recommendation, low quality of evidence) for the use of low PCT to assist clinicians in the discontinuation of empiric antibiotics when no evidence of infection is found among patients with sepsis.\n\n4. For clinical decisions regarding antibiotic use and duration, PCT has been evaluated for antibiotic initiation, antibiotic cessation, and the combination of both strategies. These strategies assume PCT availability from an institutional laboratory. If the PCT turnaround time is more than 24 hours, the effects of minimizing antimicrobial treatment days may be limited.\n\n5. It is unclear how to interpret PCT levels in certain patient populations; however, PCT use is not precluded in these populations as long as providers are aware of limitations. According to current evidence, PCT should be used with caution in the following patient populations:\n\na. Chronic kidney disease: Patients with chronic kidney disease have higher baseline levels of procalcitonin.\n\nb. PCT levels can be elevated among patients during times of noninfectious conditions such as trauma, surgery, burns, immunomodulator therapy that increases proinflammatory cytokines, cardiogenic shock, during peritoneal dialysis, and cirrhotic patients.\n\n6. According to current evidence, PCT should not routinely be measured in patients without signs and symptoms of infection. The decision to initiate patients on antibiotics without signs and symptoms of infection using PCT alone would probably lead to antimicrobial overuse and possible adverse effects associated with antimicrobial therapy. In a PCT study of critically ill patients, 1200 patients were randomized to either a PCT alert strategy or a standard of care. For those randomized to intervention, a PCT concentration greater than 1.0 mcg/L generated an alert that mandated clinical intervention, which included microbiological cultures, additional radiologic assessment, and/or initiation or expansion of antimicrobial coverage. Overall, this strategy did not lead to an improvement in mortality or time to appropriate antibiotics. In contrast, patients experienced a greater need for mechanical ventilation, prolonged ICU LOS, and prolonged antibiotic use.\n\n7. In critically ill patients with signs and symptoms of infection, a baseline PCT (at the time of the symptoms) should not be used to determine whether antibiotics should be initiated. The compliance rate for withholding antibiotics for a low PCT in this scenario has consistently been low. The compliance rate in clinical practice is likely even lower than that in clinical studies; however, this has not been evaluated. If a baseline PCT is obtained, it should be used to trend the PCT for the possible early discontinuation of antibiotics. In a study of patients with signs and symptoms of infections to determine whether a PCT-guided strategy would limit the initiation of antibiotics, no difference in antibiotic use was seen. However, this was probably because only 36% of clinicians were compliant with the recommendation to withhold antimicrobials when the PCT was low. This is in stark contrast with the 86% compliance rate with the recommendation to initiate antibiotics when the PCT was high.\n\n8. Critically ill patients with signs and symptoms of infection should have a baseline PCT obtained for trending purposes. A low PCT (or substantial decrease from baseline) during antibiotic treatment should be used to shorten the duration of antimicrobial therapy. This could be accomplished through either eliminating unnecessary antibiotics in patients who are not infected or shortening the course of therapy for patients who are infected. This strategy has been proved safe and effective in a wide spectrum of critically ill patients. Several studies have evaluated the utility of a PCT-guided strategy"}, {"page": 29, "zh": "這些研究一致顯示，PCT guidance 停用 antimicrobials 可減少 antibiotic use，且無不良 outcome 影響。已見於不同 ICU populations、不同 illness severity 與 confirmed infections 病人。最大的重症 PCT study（n=1575）發表於 2016 年，顯示 antimicrobial use（median 5 vs. 7 天）與 28-day mortality（20% vs. 25%；p=0.012）顯著降低。近期 meta-analysis 顯示，PCT-guided discontinuation 可能有 short-term mortality benefit。\n   9. 近期 prospective study 顯示，第 4 天前 PCT 未能下降至少 80%，是 mortality 的 independent predictor。\n   10. 有多種 PCT guidance algorithms；Figure 2 代表用於 antibiotic cessation 的合理 approach。某些情境會影響 PCT concentrations；例如部分 clinicians 建議，stage 5 CKD 或 dialysis 病人使用不同 cutoffs（如 >0.5 mcg/L）。某些研究對近期 surgery 者採 PCT cutoff >1.0 mcg/L。\n   11. COVID-19 病人 PCT 曾升高，但難以解讀：可能是 bacterial co-infection、ARDS severity marker，或 respiratory failure 引起 immune dysregulation，增加 cytokines production。因升高原因不明，不宜單靠 PCT 指導 antibiotic therapy。\nF. MeMed BV\n   1. 一種 host response diagnostic，可在需要時區分 bacterial 與 viral infection。以計算整合三項 host immune response proteins：TRAIL（tumor necrosis factor-related apoptosis-inducing ligand）、IP-10（interferon gamma inducible protein-10）、CRP，形成 score，表示 bacterial immune response／co-infection 相對 viral infection 的可能性。\n      a. Score：0–34 為 viral infection；35–65 不確定；66–100 為 bacterial infection。\n      b. 15 分鐘提供結果。\n   2. 廣泛 clinical implementation 前，仍需更多資料。", "en": "for determining the appropriate time to discontinue and/or de-escalate antibiotics. These studies consistently show that PCT guidance for discontinuing antimicrobial therapy led to decreases in antibiotic use without an untoward outcome effect. This has been shown in various ICU populations, in patients with different severity of illness, and in those with proven infections. The largest PCT study of critically ill patients (n=1575) was published in 2016. It demonstrated a significant decrease in the use of antimicrobials (median 5 days vs. 7 days) and 28-day mortality (20% vs. 25%; p=0.012). A recent meta-analysis showed that use of PCT to guide discontinuation of antimicrobial therapy may have a short-term mortality benefit.\n\n9. A recent prospective study showed that the inability to decrease PCT by at least 80% by day 4 was an independent predictor of mortality.\n\n10. Many different PCT guidance algorithms exist; Figure 2 represents a reasonable approach to using PCT for antibiotic cessation. In certain scenarios, PCT concentrations may be affected. For example, some clinicians recommend using different cutoffs (e.g., greater than 0.5 mcg/L) in patients with stage 5 chronic kidney disease or requiring dialysis. Furthermore, in some studies, the PCT cutoff is greater than 1.0 mcg/L among patients with recent surgery.\n\n11. Procalcitonin levels have been elevated in patients with COVID-19, although interpretation is challenging as this could represent bacterial co-infection, could be a marker of severity of acute respiratory distress syndrome, or respiratory failure could cause immune dysregulation that increases the production of cytokines. Due to the unclear cause of elevated PCT in COVID-19, it is not advisable to use the PCT level by itself to guide antibiotic therapy.\n\nF. MeMed BV\n\n1. A host response diagnostic that differentiates bacterial from viral infection at the point of need by computationally integrating the levels of three host immune response proteins (tumor necrosis factorrelated, apoptosis-inducing ligand [TRAIL], interferon gamma inducible protein-10 [IP-10], and C-reactive protein [CRP]) into a score indicating the likelihood of a bacterial immune response or coinfection versus a viral infection.\n\na. Score: 0–34 = viral infection, 35–65 = equivocal, 66–100 = bacterial infection\n\nb. Delivers results in 15 minutes\n\n2. Additional data is needed before wide spread clinical implementation"}, {"page": 30, "zh": "### Figure 2. Procalcitonin-guided Antimicrobial Management Algorithm 範例\n有 infection signs／symptoms 的病人 → 開始適當 empiric antimicrobial therapy，取得 initial PCT → empiric ABX 第 3 天：\n• 依 clinical 與 microbiological criteria 確認 infection：繼續適當 ABX，適當 de-escalation，考慮 serial PCT 決定 therapy duration。\n• Clinical suspicion of infection 不確定：取得 PCT，依結果指導 therapy；若 PCT 支持繼續 empiric ABX，考慮 daily serial PCT 決定 duration。\n• Clinical resolution 且 cultures negative，整體 infection suspicion 低：停用 empiric ABX。\nPCT 指導分支：\n|PCT 結果|建議|\n|---|---|\n|PCT <0.25 mcg/L|強烈鼓勵停止 ABX|\n|較 peak PCT 下降 ≥80%，或 PCT ≥0.25 且 <0.5 mcg/L|鼓勵停止 ABX|\n|較 peak PCT 下降 <80%，且 PCT ≥0.5 mcg/L|鼓勵繼續 ABX|\n|相較 peak concentration，PCT 增加，且 PCT ≥0.5 mcg/L|強烈鼓勵繼續或 escalation ABX|\nABX = antibiotics；PCT = procalcitonin。", "en": "Patient with signs and symptoms of infection Initiate appropriate empiric antimicrobial therapy and obtain initial PCT Day 3 of empiric ABX Confirmed diagnosis of infection through clinical and microbiological criteria Continue appropriate ABX, de-escalate as appropriate, and consider obtaining serial PCT to determine therapy duration PCT < 0.25 mcg/L Strongly encourage stopping ABX Decrease by ≥ 80% from peak PCT, or PCT ≥ 0.25 and < 0.5 mcg/L Encourage stopping ABX Decrease by < 80% from peak PCT, and PCT ≥ 0.5 mcg/L Encourage continuing ABX Increase in PCT compared with peak concentration and PCT ≥ 0.5 mcg/L Strongly encourage continuing or escalating ABX Equivocal clinical suspicion of infection Obtain PCT and use results to guide therapy. If PCT suggests continuing empiric ABX, consider obtaining serial PCT daily to determine therapy duration Overall, clinical suspicion for infections is low, given clinical resolution and negative cultures Stop empiric ABX\n\nFigure 2. Sample procalcitonin-guided antimicrobial management algorithm. ABX = antibiotics; PCT = procalcitonin."}]);
